THE REAL DADA KITCHEN

1. Take water and an onion.
2. burn them until the sun sets.
3. Serve out of a shoe.

Do this now. It is real.
dada — deterministic oracle, philosopher's stone edition
usage: ./dada [--img stone] [--poem] [command] [args...]

  (no command)      the poem
  seed              master seed (hex decimal)
  bytes <n> [s...] n hex bytes from the stone; seeds move the stream
  pick <a> <b> ...  one deterministic choice
  coin [s...]       0 or 1; seeds move it along
  roll [s...]       1..6; seeds move it along
  stream <name> <n> hex bytes from one interpretation
  interps           list the fourteen interpretations
  cell <x> <y>      one raw byte 0..255 at board x,y (wraps W x H)
  feed              a real, dead simple, dadaist recipe
  freerun [sub]     /dev/urandom — the breaking of the contract
                      freerun [n | bytes <n>]  real hex bytes
                      freerun seed | coin | roll | pick <a> <b>...
  help              this

Noise.

The scattered register knocked the last coherent thought out of noise.png.
The kernel bit into lime mortar. The sampler does not sample; the sampler scours the bottom.
The roof is a script. The script is a ridge tile.
No locks. No bus. Only clean, uninstalled grey dust settling toward zero.
